+++ b/bridge/PROTOCOL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# PSS mailbox protocol (version 1)
+
+The ROM never touches a network. It keeps a 0xA0-byte mailbox in EWRAM
+(`src/pss_net.c`); a host program reads and writes it and does the networking.
+All integers are little endian.
+
+| Offset | Size | Field | Writer | Meaning |
+|--------|------|-------|--------|---------|
+| 0x00 | 8 | magic | ROM | `PSSMBX01`. The host finds the mailbox by scanning EWRAM (0x02000000-0x0203FFFF) for this. |
+| 0x08 | 4 | version | ROM | `1` |
+| 0x0C | 4 | romSeq | ROM | Incremented after a request is fully written. |
+| 0x10 | 4 | hostSeq | host | Set to the `romSeq` value being answered, after the response is written. |
+| 0x14 | 4 | hostBeat | host | Incremented every frame while the host is alive. No change for 180 frames and the ROM shows OFFLINE. |
+| 0x18 | 1 | cmd | ROM | 1 PING, 2 HELLO, 3 PLAYER_LIST |
+| 0x19 | 1 | status | host | 0 OK, 1 ERROR, 2 UNSUPPORTED, 3 OFFLINE |
+| 0x1A | 2 | reqLen | ROM | Request payload length (max 64) |
+| 0x1C | 2 | respLen | host | Response payload length (max 64) |
+| 0x20 | 64 | req | ROM | Request payload |
+| 0x60 | 64 | resp | host | Response payload |
+
+## Handshake
+
+1. ROM writes `req`, `reqLen`, `cmd`, then increments `romSeq`.
+2. Host sees `romSeq != hostSeq`, captures `romSeq`, handles the request.
+3. Host writes `resp`, `respLen`, `status`, then sets `hostSeq` to the captured value.
+4. ROM sees `hostSeq == romSeq` and reads the response. No answer within 300 frames is a timeout.
+
+Before writing a response the host must re-read `romSeq`; if it changed, the
+ROM has moved on and the late answer must be dropped.
+
+## Payloads
+
+- `HELLO` request (16 bytes): name[8] (GBA charmap, 0xFF terminated), trainerId[4], gender[1], pad[3].
+  Response (8 bytes): sessionId[4], playersOnline[2], pad[2].
+- `PLAYER_LIST` request: empty. Response (4 + 12 x count bytes, at most 52): count[1], pad[3], then `count` entries of
+  name[8], gender[1], pad[3].
+- `PING`: empty both ways. The bridge answers it locally, so it works without a server.
+
+## Security notes
+
+Everything the server sends is untrusted. The ROM clamps lengths and strips
+control codes from names (`CopySanitizedName`). Keep that if you add commands,
+and validate any Pokémon data before it goes into the party or boxes.
